NAME
    nano — Open a file in the built-in terminal text editor.

SYNOPSIS
    nano <file>

DESCRIPTION
    The 'nano' command opens a file using the built-in terminal text editor.
    It behaves exactly like the 'edit' command and provides a familiar
    command name for users who are accustomed to nano.

    It is not actually nano. It's nano's slightly suspicious cousin.

ARGUMENTS
    file    The file to open in the terminal editor.
    Can be a relative or absolute path.

USAGE
    > nano file.txt
        Opens file.txt in the built-in terminal editor.

EXAMPLES
    > nano README.txt
        Opens README.txt for editing.

    > nano config.ini
        Opens config.ini in the terminal editor.

FUN FACTS
    - nano is simply an alias for edit.
    - Both commands use the same built-in TerminalEditor.
    - No external nano installation is required.
    - You can use whichever command feels more natural.

